From 56917f41895c6a9c9a7276f15b8a2d18f0a67932 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ond=C5=99ej=20=C5=A0imon?= <ondrej@dorhawk.software>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:56:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: Trap self-modifying code by whole host pages on
 macOS

FEX traps writes to x86 code at 4K pages, but Wine on Apple silicon has 16K
host pages: it keeps the 4K protections, yet applies their union to each host
page. A 4K page trapped read-only stayed writable while a sibling 4K page of
its host page was writable, so writes to code went unseen and FEX ran stale
translations. V8 (Microsoft 365's v8jsi.dll, x86-64) then died with "Fatal
error: unreachable code", and Outlook's "Sign in to set up Office" dialog
stayed blank.

The unix helper now reports the host page size; RWX intervals are trapped by
whole host pages, and a write fault untraps and invalidates the whole host
page. On 4K hosts nothing changes.

Proven with Gentes' harness v8jsi-script (2000 fresh functions compiled,
deoptimized and collected): 2 of 2 runs failed before, 2 of 2 pass after
(1.7 s and 1.8 s); full SMC checks also pass but take 27.4 s. Outlook's
sign-in dialog draws with default settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
